  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Suppose $n\\in\\mathbb Z$. Consider this statement: If $n$ is divisible by $12$, then $n^2$ is divisible by $12$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove this statement.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$n=12k$ gives $n^2=12(12k^2)$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$. Hence $12$ divides $n^2$.",
          "worked": "Since $12$ divides $n$, write $n=12k$ for some $k\\in\\mathbb Z$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}n^2&=(12k)^2\\\\n^2&=144k^2\\\\n^2&=12(12k^2).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $12k^2\\in\\mathbb Z$, $n^2$ is divisible by $12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Write down the converse and prove that it is not true.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Converse: If $n^2$ is divisible by $12$, then $n$ is divisible by $12$.\n\nFalse: $n=6$ gives $n^2=36$, divisible by $12$, but $6$ is not.",
          "worked": "Converse: If $n^2$ is divisible by $12$, then $n$ is divisible by $12$.\n\nTake $n=6$. Then $n^2=36=12\\times3$ is divisible by $12$, whereas $6$ is not divisible by $12$. This counterexample disproves the converse.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
